            null
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Much of it comes from the Lake District, starting at Thirlmere reservoir.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "THE *LAKE DISTRICT",
        "*THIRLMERE",
        "RESERVOIR"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "map",
        "cam": [
          -2.9,
          54.45,
          13000
        ],
        "pins": [
          [
            "THIRLMERE",
            -3.07,
            54.54,
            null
          ]
        ],
        "title": "THIRLMERE · LAKE DISTRICT"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "From there, an aqueduct carries it a hundred and fifty-three kilometres, about ninety-five miles.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "AN *AQUEDUCT",
        "*153 KILOMETRES",
        "ABOUT *95 MILES"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "stat",
        "tag": "INSTITUTION OF CIVIL ENGINEERS",
        "items": [
          {
            "v": "153",
            "suffix": " km",
            "l": "THIRLMERE TO MANCHESTER",
            "red": true
          }
        ],
        "source": "ICE"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "There are no pumps. It's the longest gravity-fed aqueduct in Britain.",
      "gap": 0.25,
      "caps": [
        "*NO PUMPS",
        "THE *LONGEST",
        "*GRAVITY-FED"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "card",
        "tag": "INSTITUTION OF CIVIL ENGINEERS",
        "l1": "NO PUMPS",
        "l2": "LONGEST IN BRITAIN",
        "source": "ICE"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "It flows at about six kilometres an hour, so it takes just over a day to arrive.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "ABOUT *6 KM/H",
        "JUST *OVER",
        "A *DAY"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "stat",
        "tag": "INSTITUTION OF CIVIL ENGINEERS",
        "items": [
          {
            "v": "6",
            "suffix": " km/h",
            "l": "FLOW SPEED",
            "red": true
          }
        ],
        "source": "ICE"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "It opened in eighteen ninety-four, and Haweswater reservoir now tops it up too.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "OPENED *1894",
        "*HAWESWATER",
        "TOPS IT *UP"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "card",
        "tag": "ICE · LAKE DISTRICT NATIONAL PARK",
        "l1": "OPENED 1894",
        "l2": "PLUS HAWESWATER",
        "source": "ICE, LAKE DISTRICT NATIONAL PARK"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "And United Utilities says most North West water is soft or very soft.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "UNITED *UTILITIES",
        "SOFT OR *VERY SOFT"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "card",
        "tag": "OFFICIAL · UNITED UTILITIES",
        "l1": "NORTH WEST WATER",
        "l2": "SOFT OR VERY SOFT",
        "source": "UNITED UTILITIES"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Where does your water come from? Comment your town.",
